WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover on-screen labels.

1a-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.988 line:4% align:center
Can a scoring method like MOSAIC's be checked

1a-2
00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:04.260 line:4% align:center
against the real world?

1b-1
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.703 line:4% align:center
Alan H. Chan and Hanrui Li, two researchers at

1b-2
00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:11.140 line:4% align:center
Columbia University, tested it from the bottom up.

2a-1
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.198 line:4% align:center
Instead of asking businesses to fill in a

2a-2
00:00:14.198 --> 00:00:16.774 line:4% align:center
questionnaire, they started with what companies

2a-3
00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:17.980 line:4% align:center
had already published.

2b-1
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.410 line:4% align:center
An AI model read each company's own

2b-2
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.248 line:4% align:center
sustainability report and answered a fixed set

2b-3
00:00:23.248 --> 00:00:25.901 line:4% align:center
of questions. The set was built on MOSAIC's

2b-4
00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.616 line:4% align:center
question bank, with extra questions for each

2b-5
00:00:28.616 --> 00:00:29.850 line:4% align:center
market and industry.

2c-1
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.691 line:4% align:center
They scored about fifteen hundred companies

2c-2
00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:35.087 line:4% align:center
listed in mainland China, almost twenty-five

2c-3
00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:37.592 line:4% align:center
hundred in Hong Kong, and around eight hundred

2c-4
00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:38.790 line:4% align:center
in the European Union.

2d-1
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.865 line:4% align:center
The rating comparisons described here focus on

2d-2
00:00:41.865 --> 00:00:43.520 line:4% align:center
mainland China and Hong Kong.

3a-1
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.377 line:4% align:center
Then they asked a simple question.

3a-2
00:00:47.377 --> 00:00:50.376 line:4% align:center
Do these scores put companies in roughly the

3a-3
00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:53.170 line:4% align:center
same order as professional ESG raters do?

3b-1
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.077 line:4% align:center
In mainland China, they compared against two

3b-2
00:00:57.077 --> 00:00:59.131 line:4% align:center
independent Chinese raters.

3b-3
00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:02.250 line:4% align:center
In Hong Kong, they compared against MSCI.

4a-1
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.524 line:4% align:center
No method matches perfectly.

4a-2
00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:07.037 line:4% align:center
Even the two Chinese raters only partly agree

4a-3
00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:07.930 line:4% align:center
with each other.

4b-1
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.443 line:4% align:center
A comparison using the MOSAIC scoring engine and

4b-2
00:01:11.443 --> 00:01:14.373 line:4% align:center
its original base weights agreed with the first

4b-3
00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:17.304 line:4% align:center
rater, on the mainland China comparison sample,

4b-4
00:01:17.304 --> 00:01:20.920 line:4% align:center
almost as closely as the two raters agree with each other.

4c-1
00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.362 line:4% align:center
Those base weights, which come from how often an

4c-2
00:01:25.362 --> 00:01:28.713 line:4% align:center
indicator recurs across established frameworks,

4c-3
00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:31.992 line:4% align:center
did better than simply weighting a question by

4c-4
00:01:31.992 --> 00:01:34.060 line:4% align:center
how many companies report it.

4d-1
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:38.062 line:4% align:center
In a separate re-reading of fifty reports, using

4d-2
00:01:38.062 --> 00:01:41.580 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC's graded answer scales produced closer

4d-3
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.098 line:4% align:center
agreement with external ratings than reducing

4d-4
00:01:45.098 --> 00:01:46.740 line:4% align:center
answers to yes or no.

5a-1
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.565 line:4% align:center
The team also designed their own weighting,

5a-2
00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:53.391 line:4% align:center
which gives greater weight to disclosures

5a-3
00:01:53.391 --> 00:01:56.425 line:4% align:center
associated with third-party verification and

5a-4
00:01:56.425 --> 00:02:00.010 line:4% align:center
measured quantities. It is not part of MOSAIC today.

5b-1
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.062 line:4% align:center
Their alternative weighting increased agreement

5b-2
00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:06.110 line:4% align:center
with the external raters in the reported comparisons.

5c-1
00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:10.263 line:4% align:center
In Hong Kong, agreement with MSCI was weaker for

5c-2
00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.190 line:4% align:center
every method they tried.

6a-1
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.785 line:4% align:center
These results have limits, and the authors state

6a-2
00:02:15.785 --> 00:02:16.520 line:4% align:center
them plainly.

6b-1
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.660 line:4% align:center
These were listed companies, not small businesses.

6c-1
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.770 line:4% align:center
The scores were compared with other ratings, not

6c-2
00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.220 line:4% align:center
with what later happened to the companies.

6d-1
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.688 line:4% align:center
Two AI readings of the same reports agreed on

6d-2
00:02:28.688 --> 00:02:30.460 line:4% align:center
most answers, but not all.

6e-1
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.845 line:4% align:center
Weights estimated in mainland China were carried

6e-2
00:02:33.845 --> 00:02:37.080 line:4% align:center
over to Hong Kong without being re-estimated there.

6f-1
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.122 line:4% align:center
And the study tested MOSAIC's questions, weights

6f-2
00:02:41.122 --> 00:02:44.450 line:4% align:center
and scoring. It did not test how MOSAIC builds

6f-3
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.705 line:4% align:center
its question bank, sets its configuration, or

6f-4
00:02:47.705 --> 00:02:49.730 line:4% align:center
selects evidence for advice.

7a-1
00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:53.867 line:4% align:center
These comparisons provide encouraging evidence

7a-2
00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:56.749 line:4% align:center
for elements of the MOSAIC scoring design,

7a-3
00:02:56.749 --> 00:02:59.425 line:4% align:center
particularly its base weights, category

7a-4
00:02:59.425 --> 00:03:01.827 line:4% align:center
structure and graded answer scales.

7a-5
00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:05.190 line:4% align:center
They also identify opportunities for improvement.

7b-1
00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.515 line:4% align:center
They do not yet establish how well the current

7b-2
00:03:08.515 --> 00:03:10.778 line:4% align:center
SME application predicts real-world

7b-3
00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:12.524 line:4% align:center
sustainability performance.

7b-4
00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.369 line:4% align:center
The authors recommend testing scores against

7b-5
00:03:15.369 --> 00:03:17.180 line:4% align:center
subsequent company outcomes.

7c-1
00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.370 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
